package com.chordx.app.data

import java.time.LocalDate

/** A verse for the day, with a short insight. Text is the King James Version (public domain). */
data class DailyVerse(val reference: String, val text: String, val insight: String)

object DailyVerses {
    /** The same verse all day, rotating through the list; no network needed. */
    fun forDate(date: LocalDate): DailyVerse = all[Math.floorMod(date.toEpochDay(), all.size.toLong()).toInt()]

    val all: List<DailyVerse> = listOf(
        DailyVerse("Psalm 119:105", "Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path.",
            "A lamp lights the next step, not the whole road. God usually shows us enough for today and asks us to trust Him with tomorrow. What step is in front of you today?"),
        DailyVerse("Proverbs 3:5-6", "Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding. In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.",
            "Trust is a whole-heart decision, and it is tested where our own understanding runs out. Acknowledging God in every way means inviting Him into the ordinary choices, not just the big ones."),
        DailyVerse("Philippians 4:6-7", "Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God. And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.",
            "Anxiety is met with prayer and thanksgiving, not willpower. Notice that peace is promised as a guard over your heart and mind, even before the situation changes."),
        DailyVerse("Isaiah 41:10", "Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.",
            "God answers fear with His presence first, then His help. Every promise here is something He does, not something we must produce."),
        DailyVerse("Romans 8:28", "And we know that all things work together for good to them that love God, to them who are the called according to his purpose.",
            "This does not say every event is good, but that God weaves all of them toward a good purpose for those who love Him. It invites us to hold hard seasons with hope."),
        DailyVerse("Joshua 1:9", "Have not I commanded thee? Be strong and of a good courage; be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest.",
            "Courage here is rooted in a reason: God goes with you wherever you go. Strength is not the absence of fear but obedience in spite of it."),
        DailyVerse("Psalm 23:1-3", "The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want. He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters. He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name's sake.",
            "A shepherd provides, rests and guides. Where do you need to let Him lead you to rest today, rather than pushing on alone?"),
        DailyVerse("Matthew 6:33", "But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.",
            "Priorities shape the day. Putting God first does not remove our needs; it places them under His care."),
        DailyVerse("John 3:16", "For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.",
            "Love is shown by giving. God's gift is open to whoever believes, which means no one is too far gone and no one is left out."),
        DailyVerse("Jeremiah 29:11", "For I know the thoughts that I think toward you, saith the LORD, thoughts of peace, and not of evil, to give you an expected end.",
            "Spoken to people in exile, this is a promise of hope in a waiting season. God's plans are good even when the present feels far from home."),
        DailyVerse("Isaiah 40:31", "But they that wait upon the LORD shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint.",
            "Waiting on the Lord is active trust, and strength is renewed in the waiting. Even walking steadily without fainting is a gift worth asking for."),
        DailyVerse("Matthew 11:28", "Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.",
            "Jesus invites the weary to come to Him, not to try harder. What burden can you hand over today?"),
        DailyVerse("Psalm 46:1", "God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.",
            "God is not a distant help. He is present and near in trouble, and He is both a place to hide and a source of strength."),
        DailyVerse("Romans 12:2", "And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.",
            "Change begins in the mind. Daily time in Scripture is one of the ways God renews how we think, so that we can recognise His will."),
        DailyVerse("2 Corinthians 5:7", "For we walk by faith, not by sight.",
            "Faith is a way of walking, one step at a time, without needing to see everything first. Where is God asking you to trust Him beyond what you can see?"),
        DailyVerse("Philippians 4:13", "I can do all things through Christ which strengtheneth me.",
            "Paul wrote this about contentment in every circumstance, plenty or need. Christ's strength carries us through what He has called us to, not whatever we choose."),
        DailyVerse("Psalm 27:1", "The LORD is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the LORD is the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?",
            "Light, salvation and strength: David lists what God is to him before asking what there is to fear. Remembering who God is shrinks our fears."),
        DailyVerse("Hebrews 11:1", "Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.",
            "Faith is confidence in what God has promised, even while it is still unseen. It is not wishful thinking; it rests on His character."),
        DailyVerse("Colossians 3:23", "And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men;",
            "Ordinary work becomes worship when it is done for the Lord. Whom are you really serving in what you do today?"),
        DailyVerse("1 Thessalonians 5:16-18", "Rejoice evermore. Pray without ceasing. In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.",
            "Joy, prayer and thanks are described here as God's will for us. They are a rhythm to practise through the day, not only in good moments."),
        DailyVerse("James 1:5", "If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.",
            "God gives wisdom generously and without scolding us for asking. What decision do you need wisdom for today?"),
        DailyVerse("Micah 6:8", "He hath shewed thee, O man, what is good; and what doth the LORD require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?",
            "God's requirements are clear and lived out in relationships: act fairly, love kindness, walk humbly with Him."),
        DailyVerse("Lamentations 3:22-23", "It is of the LORD's mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not. They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness.",
            "Written in the middle of grief, this is a reminder that God's mercy is renewed each morning. Today does not run on yesterday's mercy."),
        DailyVerse("Psalm 37:4", "Delight thyself also in the LORD; and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart.",
            "Delighting in God shapes what we desire. As we draw close to Him, our wants begin to line up with His good purposes."),
        DailyVerse("Matthew 5:16", "Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.",
            "The aim of good works is that others see God, not us. Where can your light be seen today at home, at church or at work?"),
        DailyVerse("1 Peter 5:7", "Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.",
            "We are invited to hand over our cares because He genuinely cares. What are you still carrying that you could cast on Him?"),
        DailyVerse("Ephesians 2:8-9", "For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any man should boast.",
            "Salvation is a gift, which frees us from earning and from comparing. Gratitude, not pride, is the natural response."),
        DailyVerse("Psalm 34:8", "O taste and see that the LORD is good: blessed is the man that trusteth in him.",
            "Goodness is something we experience, not just agree with. Take a moment to recall a way God has been good to you recently."),
        DailyVerse("John 15:5", "I am the vine, ye are the branches: He that abideth in me, and I in him, the same bringeth forth much fruit: for without me ye can do nothing.",
            "Fruit grows from staying connected, not from striving. Abiding means making time for Jesus before doing for Jesus."),
        DailyVerse("Galatians 5:22-23", "But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith, Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.",
            "Fruit is the Spirit's work in us over time. Which of these do you most need to ask Him to grow today?"),
        DailyVerse("Proverbs 16:3", "Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established.",
            "Committing our work to God steadies our thinking. Hand today's plans to Him before you start."),
        DailyVerse("Psalm 91:1-2", "He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty. I will say of the LORD, He is my refuge and my fortress: my God; in him will I trust.",
            "Dwelling is more than visiting. Staying close to God is how we know Him as refuge, and we say it out loud: He is my fortress."),
        DailyVerse("2 Timothy 1:7", "For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind.",
            "Fear does not come from God. What He gives is power, love and a clear mind, which are what we need to face what scares us."),
        DailyVerse("Romans 5:8", "But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.",
            "God's love did not wait for us to improve. Resting in being loved already is the starting point for everything else."),
        DailyVerse("Isaiah 26:3", "Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.",
            "Peace follows where the mind is fixed. When your thoughts race today, bring them back to who God is."),
        DailyVerse("John 14:27", "Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be afraid.",
            "Jesus leaves us His own peace, which does not depend on circumstances. It is a gift to receive, not a feeling to manufacture."),
        DailyVerse("Psalm 100:4-5", "Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, and into his courts with praise: be thankful unto him, and bless his name. For the LORD is good; his mercy is everlasting; and his truth endureth to all generations.",
            "Thanksgiving is the way in to worship. Name specific things you are thankful for before you bring requests."),
        DailyVerse("Matthew 7:7", "Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you:",
            "Ask, seek, knock: persistent prayer is encouraged, not discouraged. What have you stopped asking God for?"),
        DailyVerse("Deuteronomy 31:6", "Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for the LORD thy God, he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.",
            "Moses said this to people about to face a battle he would not join. God's promise to go with them, and with us, does not fail."),
        DailyVerse("1 John 4:19", "We love him, because he first loved us.",
            "Our love for God is a response, not an achievement. Remembering how He loved us first makes loving others easier."),
        DailyVerse("Psalm 121:1-2", "I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help. My help cometh from the LORD, which made heaven and earth.",
            "The psalmist looks past the hills to the One who made them. Our help comes from the Creator, not from the circumstances we are looking at."),
    )
}
